# A small markdown: blocks of lines, with inline code and emphasis.
#
# Authored as a presentation fixture — the third demonstrator language beside
# a JSON and an ABNF formulation — so a ceiling can be written against a
# document format whose whole point is how it DRAWS.
#
# Unambiguous by construction, which costs two restrictions worth stating.
# A paragraph's first character cannot be `#` or `-`, because those open a
# heading and a bullet: without that, "# x" derives two ways (a heading, and a
# paragraph whose text begins with a hash), and two derivations that mean
# different things are refused by both engines rather than silently picked.
# And a line interleaves plain runs with styled ones rather than repeating a
# chunk, because two adjacent plain runs would carve one run of text two ways.

document ::= block+

block ::= heading | bullet | paragraph | blank

heading   ::= level " " line "\n"
bullet    ::= "- " line "\n"
paragraph ::= start line "\n"
blank     ::= "\n"

level  ::= "#"+
start  ::= opener | styled
opener ::= [^#\-*`\n]
line   ::= plain? (styled plain?)*

styled   ::= code | emphasis
code     ::= "`" plain "`"
emphasis ::= "*" plain "*"
plain    ::= [^*`\n]+
